# Discovery: LLM-driven agent loop

## The loop

```
loop (until done / maxSteps / timeout / stuck / policy-block):
  obs   = surface.observe()             // compressed a11y snapshot + url +
                                         // last action result
  call  = llm.act(goal, obs, history)   // strict tool call, not free-form JSON
  gate  = policy.check(call)            // rejection is fed back to the model
                                         // as a tool result, not a crash
  res   = surface.execute(call)         // mechanically capture the FULL set
                                         // of locator candidates for the
                                         // acted-on element
  recorder.push({call, resolvedLocatorCandidates,
                 obsHashBefore, obsHashAfter})
```

## Tools (the model's action space)

`navigate(url)` / `click(ref)` / `fill(ref, text)` / `select(ref, option)` /
`press(key)` / `extract(ref, outputName)` / `wait_for(text|ref)` /
`report_business_outcome(code, evidence)` /
`escalate(reason, what_human_should_do)` /
`done(summary, checkpointDescription, outputs)`

The model acts only by `ref` — never by inventing a selector string. This is
what eliminates locator hallucination; see invariants.mdc rule #2.

## Stuck / stopping conditions (must be real, not a TODO)

- `maxSteps` (default 25) or wall-clock timeout
- **No progress:** 3 consecutive observations hash identically
- **Loop:** the same `(action, ref)` pair repeats ≥2 times
- PolicyGate rejects consecutive actions
- The model calls `escalate` itself
- The run exceeds `MAX_RUN_TOKENS` (see cost-control.mdc)

Any of these must produce an `InterventionRequest` and hand off to the human
escalation flow (see escalation-spec.mdc) — not just abort silently.

## Compiling the recording into an artifact

Two phases — see schema-spec.mdc "Compilation" for the full contract:

1. **Mechanical (no LLM):** turn each recorded action into a `Step`. Locators
   come only from what was captured off the real element at execution time.
2. **Annotation (LLM, Zod-validated output):** the model only proposes input
   parameterization, step `intent` text, the `successCheckpoint`, and
   candidate `outcomes`. Validation failure → retry once → fall back to a
   mechanical-only artifact with `status: "draft"`.

## LLM client discipline

- All calls go through `src/llm/client.ts`. Never call the Anthropic SDK
  directly from `loop.ts`, `compiler.ts`, or anywhere else.
- Respect `LLM_MODE` (`auto` | `replay` | `live`) — see cost-control.mdc.
- The observation format sent to the model is the compressed accessibility
  snapshot from `Surface.observe()`, not raw HTML and not a screenshot by
  default.
